# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings regardless of the checkout platform's
# autocrlf setting — a CRLF-corrupted shebang/script breaks execution and
# reintroduces the exact CRLF-parsing bugs these scripts guard against
# (see nestjs-project/scripts/env-check.sh's .env.example parsing).
*.sh text eol=lf

# TypeScript sources must check out as LF regardless of the checkout platform's
# autocrlf setting — without this, Windows checkouts get CRLF and fail
# `prettier --check` project-wide (KI-2, docs/known-issues.md).
*.ts text eol=lf
